ts","k":"have has had give gave live live cone of silence; vowel vault in gave "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 9: The vault","u":"steps/09.html","s":"Jobs across letters","k":"make like time home name the vault on every vowel–consonant–e word "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 10: The nice-nudge","u":"steps/10.html","s":"Jobs across letters","k":"nice face place age page huge nice-nudge "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 11: Vowel teams","u":"steps/11.html","s":"Jobs across letters","k":"may day see been might night none "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 12: The r-controlled unit","u":"steps/12.html","s":"Jobs across letters","k":"or for her are were car bird turn r-controlled unit "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 13: A suffix joins at the seam","u":"steps/13.html","s":"Morphemes","k":"gets sees going doing being played morpheme seam "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 14: The box blocks the vault","u":"steps/14.html","s":"Morphemes","k":"spell spelling get getting help helped sun sunny happy block box and blocked vault, where two consonants stop a reach, doubled or already there (spelling, getting, helped) "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 15: The e drops, its jobs move","u":"steps/15.html","s":"Morphemes","k":"make making have having race racing ice icy none: the vault and nudge move to the suffix vowel "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 16: Open and closed in longer words","u":"steps/16.html","s":"Single vowels","k":"silent tiger paper music open over none: the vault reaches across the syllable, and a weak vowel stays bare silent/silly, open/seven"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 17: Consonant + le","u":"steps/17.html","s":"Single vowels","k":"table bugle title little apple middle none: a red bond bar and one red circle under le "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 18: Long before two consonants","u":"steps/18.html","s":"Single vowels","k":"old cold both most only find kind child wild none: the long mark with no vault most/cost, mind/mint"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 19: A vowel that borrows a sound","u":"steps/19.html","s":"Single vowels","k":"come some done from was what do to who does none: the borrowing vowel stays bare home/come, bone/done/gone"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 20: Teams for the long vowels","u":"steps/20.html","s":"Vowel teams","k":"rain paid eat read please boat show grow own pie they eight none "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 21: The long u sound","u":"steps/21.html","s":"Vowel teams","k":"too moon food new grew blue true you soup none do/due/dew"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 22: A team's second sound","u":"steps/22.html","s":"Vowel teams","k":"look good book head bread put pull said again many open: whether a team with two sounds takes a mark moon/book, eat/head"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 23: The aw sound","u":"steps/23.html","s":"Vowel teams","k":"saw draw law because want wash water all small walk none "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 24: The ouch and oil sounds","u":"steps/24.html","s":"More units","k":"out round found how now down coin point boy toy none: ow joins the teams with two sounds now/snow"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 25: Silent letters join their unit","u":"steps/25.html","s":"More units","k":"know knee knife write wrong lamb climb two black bond bar for a consonant unit knot/not, wrap/rap"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 26: More r-controlled units","u":"steps/26.html","s":"More units","k":"hair hear our your their more before care there where none: the red bar runs under three letters in hair. Our splits into the ou of out and an r. were/there, are/care"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 27: Two words join","u":"steps/27.html","s":"Families","k":"I'm it's isn't don't can't won't we're red apostrophe for the letters left out "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 28: The th and wh family","u":"steps/28.html","s":"Families","k":"this that these those then there proposed: pointer pill then/when, there/where, that/what"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 29: -y, -ly and y turns to i","u":"steps/29.html","s":"Families","k":"sadly slowly happily happier tried carries none: the seam try/tried, play/played"},{"t":"step","l":"Step 30: un- and re-","u":"steps/30.html","s":"Families","k":"undo untie unhappy unlock redo replay refill reread none: the seam, before the root "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 31: A Latin family: act and create","u":"steps/31.html","s":"Families","k":"act action actor active react create creation creator none "},{"t":"step","l":"Step 32: A Greek family: photo, phone, graph","u":"steps/32.html","s":"Families","k":"photo phone graph telephone photograph alphabet none: the black bond bar under ph "},{"t":"mark","l":"Sound circle","u":"notations.html#mark-sound-circle","s":"drawn on this","k":"One circle under each sound: red for a vowel sound, black for a consonant, green for sh, th, ch and the sh of -tion"},{"t":"mark","l":"Syllable swoop","u":"notations.html#mark-syllable-swoop","s":"drawn on happy","k":"One swoop under each syllable"},{"t":"mark","l":"Short mark","u":"notations.html#mark-short-mark","s":"drawn on get","k":"A cup over a vowel that keeps its short sound"},{"t":"mark","l":"Long mark","u":"notations.html#mark-long-mark","s":"drawn on go","k":"A bar over a vowel that says its name"},{"t":"mark","l":"Bond bar","u":"notations.html#mark-bond-bar","s":"drawn on teaching","k":"A bar under letters that work as one unit, most of them spelling one sound: black for consonant units and for doubled letters, boxed or not, green for sh, th, ch and the ti of -tion, red for vowel units. The letters keep their own colours. Qu is the consonant unit with two sounds: the bar ties the q to the u it always comes with, and a circle under each letter counts the k and the w"},{"t":"mark","l":"R-controlled unit","u":"notations.html#mark-r-controlled-unit","s":"drawn on car","k":"A red bar under a vowel and its r, with the vowel red, the r black and one circle"},{"t":"mark","l":"Block box","u":"notations.html#mark-block-box","s":"drawn on hopping","k":"A box around the vowel protector at work: a pair or cluster with a vowel after it, which it stops from reaching back. A pair keeps its bond bar when the box comes; a cluster has none"},{"t":"mark","l":"Cone of silence","u":"notations.html#mark-cone-of-silence","s":"drawn on have","k":"A dotted ring around a silent e"},{"t":"mark","l":"Vowel vault","u":"notations.html#mark-vowel-vault","s":"drawn on make","k":"An arc from an e, or a vowel after one consonant, back to the vowel it makes long"},{"t":"mark","l":"Nice-nudge","u":"notations.html#mark-nice-nudge","s":"drawn on nice","k":"A small arc under the letters from e, i or y to the c or g it softens"},{"t":"mark","l":"Blocked vault","u":"notations.html#mark-blocked-vault","s":"drawn on getting","k":"A half-arc that ends in a red X where a box stops the vault"},{"t":"mark","l":"Morpheme seam","u":"notations.html#mark-morpheme-seam","s":"drawn on going","k":"A dotted line between morphemes"},{"t":"term","l":"legomorphic","u":"definitions.html#def-legomorphic","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"legomorph","u":"definitions.html#def-legomorph","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"legomorphics","u":"definitions.html#def-legomorphics","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"Legomorphic Notation","u":"definitions.html#def-legomorphic-notation","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"kernel","u":"definitions.html#def-kernel","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"actor","u":"definitions.html#def-actor","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"action","u":"definitions.html#def-action","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"acted-on","u":"definitions.html#def-acted-on","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"operator","u":"definitions.html#def-operator","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"modal","u":"definitions.html#def-modal","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"query","u":"definitions.html#def-query","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"claim","u":"definitions.html#def-claim","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"question","u":"definitions.html#def-question","s":"Definitions","x":1},{"t":"term","l":"flip","u":"definitions.html#def-flip","s":"Definitions","x